          "annotations": [],
          "text": "{\"stories\":[{\"id\":\"s000029\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":6,\"style\":5,\"grammar\":8,\"storytelling\":6,\"overall\":6},\"note\":\"The fair-sharing problem resolves visibly with buns and a new label, but repeated explanations and an unclear initial label issue make it feel procedural.\"},{\"id\":\"s000057\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":6,\"style\":5,\"grammar\":8,\"storytelling\":6,\"overall\":6},\"note\":\"Ada checks, gets permission, and gives Noor a suitable bun, but the scale does not meaningfully determine the outcome and the prose repeats its accounting.\"},{\"id\":\"s000047\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":5,\"style\":5,\"grammar\":8,\"storytelling\":5,\"overall\":5},\"note\":\"The label is found accurate, yet the ending calls it a fresh label and says there was no label to trust, creating a central contradiction despite a concrete resolution.\"},{\"id\":\"s000073\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":5,\"style\":5,\"grammar\":8,\"storytelling\":5,\"overall\":5},\"note\":\"Ada discovers the label is inaccurate but later sets out a checked label whose words match the buns without showing how it was corrected; the bun-sharing ending is otherwise clear.\"},{\"id\":\"s000034\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":5,\"style\":5,\"grammar\":8,\"storytelling\":5,\"overall\":5},\"note\":\"The accurate-label discovery conflicts with the final claim that a fresh label was made because none could be trusted; permission also arrives after Ada has placed Noor's bun.\"},{\"id\":\"s000043\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":6,\"style\":5,\"grammar\":8,\"storytelling\":6,\"overall\":6},\"note\":\"The sequence reaches a fair, concrete outcome—berry bun, reserved nut bun, clear label—but it relies on repetitive explanatory wording rather than dramatic action.\"},{\"id\":\"s000068\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":4,\"style\":5,\"grammar\":8,\"storytelling\":5,\"overall\":5},\"note\":\"The same label is called inaccurate and then treated as a checked matching label, while Pip chooses the nut bun only after the conclusion says it remained his; the ending image works.\"},{\"id\":\"s000096\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":5,\"style\":5,\"grammar\":8,\"storytelling\":5,\"overall\":5},\"note\":\"Ada gives Noor the berry bun before Mara grants permission to arrange the share, weakening causality; the physical final arrangement is clear but heavily restated.\"},{\"id\":\"s000005\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":5,\"style\":5,\"grammar\":8,\"storytelling\":5,\"overall\":5},\"note\":\"It has a clear need and a visible sharing resolution, but an inaccurate label becomes a matching checked label without a shown correction, and much of the prose is repetitive.\"},{\"id\":\"s000085\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":5,\"style\":5,\"grammar\":8,\"storytelling\":5,\"overall\":5},\"note\":\"Noor receives a safe berry bun and the display is clarified, but Mara's permission follows Ada's action and the label is replaced without the original problem being concretely established.\"}],\"diversity\":{\"premise\":1,\"causal_path\":2,\"ending\":1,\"language\":2,\"overall\":1},\"diversity_evidence\":\"All ten stories use the same market-stall problem: Ada checks confusing bun information, protects Pip's nut bun, gives Noor a suitable bun, and ends with a clear display. Minor changes—plain versus berry bun, accurate versus inaccurate label, tasting versus weighing, and timing of permission—do not create materially distinct plots (s000029, s000057, s000047, s000073, s000034, s000043, s000068, s000096, s000005, s000085). This sample does not establish the diversity of the entire generator.\",\"plot_groups\":[{\"story_ids\":[\"s000029\",\"s000057\",\"s000047\",\"s000073\",\"s000034\",\"s000043\",\"s000068\",\"s000096\",\"s000005\",\"s000085\"],\"summary\":\"Ada investigates bun information and Noor's needs, preserves Pip's nut bun, assigns Noor a suitable bun, and clarifies the stall label; variations are only in evidence steps, order, and wording.\"}]}",
          "type": "output_text",
